<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gennaro Annese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1604–<a href="/years/1648">1648</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gennaro Annese was a Neapolitan gunsmith who became a leader of the revolt against Spanish rule after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masaniello">Masaniello</a>. In October 1647 he proclaimed the Neapolitan Republic and invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-guise">Henry II, Duke of Guise</a>, to protect it. He came to terms with the Spanish when they retook the city in April 1648, but was executed later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gennaro-annese.jpg" alt="Gennaro Annese" width="300" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aniello Falcone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Annese.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
